.TH KIWAMI 1 "2026" "kiwami" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kiwami \- small window that identifies file types and handles renaming, attributes, timestamps and archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiwami
[\fB\-\-new\-window\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiwami
(Japanese name: 極み窓) opens a small, always-on-top window. Drop files or folders onto it to see
what a file really contains (detected from its content, not its name) and whether its extension matches.
It can fix wrong extensions, rename files, change permissions and timestamps (with undo), show text,
images, hex dumps and archive listings, and create or extract zip, 7z, tar.gz and tar.xz archives.
.PP
If kiwami is already running, the given files are added to the existing window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Always open a new window instead of passing the files to a running kiwami.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kiwami/types.json
User dictionary of file types (Japanese names, extensions, signatures).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/kiwami/history.json
Recently handled files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1),
.BR 7z (1),
.BR unrar (1)
